<title>GERMANY: Allianz Life 4-month premiums up 5.1 pct.</title>
<headline>Allianz Life 4-month premiums up 5.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STUTTGART, Germany 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Four months to April 30</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Premium income			     4,100  up 5.1 pct</p>
<p>    New premiums				 970    up 6.4 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German insurance group is Allianz Lebensversicherungs AG, the life insurance arm of Allianz AG Holding.</p>
<p>Allianz Life Chairman Gerhard Rupprecht said in a speech prepared for the company's shareholder meeting that new business largely consisted of private pension contracts.</p>
<p>The overall outlook for German life insurance had been boosted by escalating demand for private pensions, he said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
